# PRODUCT DEVELOPMENT PROPOSAL
**Project:** Fleet Tracking & Dispatch Management Platform  
**Target Delivery:** Driver & Rider Mobile Tracking App (Android & iOS via React Native / Expo) + Master Web Control Dashboard (Next.js)  
**Prepared By:** Trade Infrastructure LTD (Sales Cowboy)  
**Date:** November 10, 2026  

---

## 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE
To develop a streamlined, lightweight logistics tracking and dispatch system for a transport and courier company. 

The system turns the rider or driver's smartphone into a live GPS tracker via a dedicated mobile app, streaming location updates in the background. The business owner and dispatch managers retain full visibility and control via a central web dashboard, allowing them to monitor active routes, assign delivery jobs, and manage driver operational status in real time.

---

## 2. FUNCTIONAL SYSTEM MODULES

### Module 1: Driver & Rider Mobile Tracking App (React Native / Expo - Android & iOS)
* **Driver Authentication & Shift Toggle:**
  * Simple phone/email login with SMS OTP verification.
  * One-tap `Start Shift (Online)` and `End Shift (Offline)` toggle.
* **Background GPS Location Streaming:**
  * Transmits real-time GPS coordinates (latitude, longitude, speed, heading) while the rider is online.
  * Battery-optimized location pings designed for low data consumption on Nigerian mobile networks.
* **Assigned Delivery Tasks:**
  * Clean task list displaying pending deliveries, pickup addresses, recipient phone contacts, and delivery destinations.
  * One-tap customer call button.
  * Task progression buttons: `Accept Task` -> `Arrived at Pickup` -> `En Route` -> `Delivered`.
* **Turn-by-Turn Route Handoff:** One-touch button opening external navigation (Google Maps / Apple Maps) directly to the delivery drop-off point.

### Module 2: Central Fleet Control Web Dashboard (Next.js)
* **Live Fleet Tracking Map:**
  * Interactive map (Leaflet / OpenStreetMap) showing all active riders, live vehicle locations, and current availability status (Available, Busy on Delivery, Offline).
  * Click on any vehicle marker to view driver identity, current speed, battery level, and assigned order reference.
* **Dispatch & Task Assignment Desk:**
  * Create delivery orders: pickup location, delivery address, package description, customer name, and contact details.
  * Assign orders manually to the closest available rider or broadcast for pickup.
* **Driver & Vehicle Master Directory:**
  * Register and manage rider profiles (full name, phone number, vehicle type, license plate number).
  * Activate, reassign, or suspend driver access in one click.
* **Trip History & Completed Logs:** Searchable archive of past deliveries, completion timestamps, assigned riders, and delivery proof records.

